# The desktop: niri, with a Quickshell shell, behind greetd. Its per-user
# configuration comes from /usr through user-tmpfiles
# (usr/share/user-tmpfiles.d/80-desktop.conf), or natively from /etc/xdg.

# Graphics: Mesa, Vulkan for AMD, virtio (VMs) and the software fallback.
mesa
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-virtio
vulkan-swrast

niri
xwayland-satellite
quickshell
greetd
fuzzel
mako
wl-mirror

